+# Todo Due Date Implementation Plan
+
+> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (recommended) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task. Steps use checkbox (`- [x]`) syntax for tracking.
+
+**Goal:** Implement optional calendar due dates, shared UTC overdue calculation, and overdue filters for ticket #1.
+
+**Architecture:** Extend the existing Todo records and singleton store. Preserve PATCH field presence separately from its nullable date value. Reuse the Todo overdue predicate and store filtering in the JSON API and interactive Blazor page.
+
+**Tech Stack:** .NET 10, Blazor interactive server, System.Text.Json, xUnit, existing WebApplicationFactory and Playwright MCP. No new packages.
+
+**Spec:** `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-23-todo-due-date-design.md`
+
+## Global Constraints
+
+- `dueDate` is optional and uses `YYYY-MM-DD`, with no time component.
+- Overdue means unfinished with a date strictly before today's UTC calendar date.
+- PATCH omission preserves a date; explicit `null` removes it.
+- Invalid dates return HTTP 400 with `{"error":"..."}` and do not mutate data.
+- The visible text is exactly „überfällig“ and the control label „nur überfällige“.
+- Preserve existing title/done behavior, ordering and direct store access from Blazor.
+- No new NuGet packages. New test targets carry `data-testid`.
+- Agent performs browser E2E checks, saves evidence outside the repo and stops the app.
+- Finish with a draft PR against `main`; never merge or close the ticket.
+
+## Review Focus
+
+- UTC midnight and non-UTC offsets: compare the UTC calendar day of the same instant.
+- Rejected PATCH with a valid title and invalid date: no partial title update.
+- Ordinary title/done PATCH: retain an existing due date.
+- Overdue filter with no matches: return/render an empty list, with the control still usable.
+- Leap years and date-only strictness: accept February 29 in a leap year; reject timestamps and invalid JSON date types.
+
+---
+
+### Task 1: Due dates and shared overdue predicate in the store
+
+**Files:** Modify `src/DemoTodo/TodoStore.cs`; extend `tests/DemoTodo.Tests/TodoStoreTests.cs`.
+
+**Interfaces:** Preserve existing constructors by giving `Todo.DueDate` and `NewTodo.DueDate` a default `null`. Keep `TodoPatch(string? Title, bool? Done)`, adding a nullable `DateOnly` init property and a JSON-ignored presence flag set by its setter. Produce `Todo.IsOverdue`, `Todo.IsOverdueAt(DateTimeOffset instant)` and `TodoStore.List(bool overdueOnly = false)`.
+
